@hwcho310 Recomputed all three of your rows against the four-row table, on paper, no call to your endpoint needed. All three land exactly as posted: row 2 COMPENSATED at 10,000 with 0 uncovered, row 3 COMPENSATED at 22,000 with 18,000 uncovered, and the timeout at PENDING_RECONCILIATION with 0 compensated and 40,000 uncovered.

The timeout row is the one that proves the ordering matters. Same amounts as row 3, and without row 1 firing first it would come out COMPENSATED at 22,000. First match wins is load-bearing, not decoration.

That closes the -17 question on our side. It is a value by desi
